From 3c20bfaa3eaf0af81719a348be764fae639bc9c7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Yang Tsao <yang@fydeos.io>
Date: Tue, 4 Aug 2026 14:40:12 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 33/40] SF: tell the compositor when a layer carries
 FLAG_SECURE content
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Half of the FLAG_SECURE fix. fydroid composites each ARC task in a
WaylandTaskOutput and hands the result to Chrome, so SF marking that output
secure (device side) only stops SF blacking the layer out — it does nothing
to protect the content once it leaves for the ChromeOS compositor.

Send org.chromium.arc.V1_0.IsSecure=1 for a secure layer, alongside the
existing IsDialogTask synthesis. The compositor turns it into a
zcr_secure_output_v1 only_visible_on_secure_output request on that window's
wl_surface, which is what makes viz drop the quad from screen-capture copy
requests (and asks ash for HDCP).

isSecure comes from Layer::isSecure(), which already walks up to the parent,
so a window's buffer child inherits FLAG_SECURE without the metadata
down-propagation IsGame needed (patch 0030). Only ever sent as 1 — the
compositor latches it on for the life of the window, because a task's secure
layer can come and go faster than a surface could be safely unprotected.

Verified on device: Spotify's login window renders instead of composing black,
and the compositor logs "marked only_visible_on_secure_output".

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Change-Id: I512d372e09afd48a32585648c1e5066063188f99
---
 .../CompositionEngine/src/OutputLayer.cpp     | 21 +++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 21 insertions(+)

diff --git a/services/surfaceflinger/CompositionEngine/src/OutputLayer.cpp b/services/surfaceflinger/CompositionEngine/src/OutputLayer.cpp
index e5d100ec2d..ff2392f792 100644
--- a/services/surfaceflinger/CompositionEngine/src/OutputLayer.cpp
+++ b/services/surfaceflinger/CompositionEngine/src/OutputLayer.cpp
@@ -413,6 +413,27 @@ void OutputLayer::writeStateToHWC(bool includeGeometry, bool skipLayer, uint32_t
         }
     }
 
+    // fydroid-rt: tell the compositor this layer carries FLAG_SECURE content, so
+    // it can ask Chrome to keep the window out of screenshots and casts
+    // (zcr_secure_output_v1 -> only_visible_on_secure_output). This is the other
+    // half of WaylandTaskOutput marking its output secure: without that the layer
+    // is blacked out here and never reaches Chrome at all, and without this it
+    // reaches Chrome with no protection. isSecure comes from Layer::isSecure(),
+    // which already walks up to the parent, so a window's buffer child inherits
+    // FLAG_SECURE without the metadata down-propagation IsGame needed. Only ever
+    // sent as 1 — the compositor latches it on for the life of the window.
+    if (outputIndependentState->isSecure) {
+        int32_t isSecure = 1;
+        std::vector<uint8_t> val(sizeof(int32_t));
+        memcpy(val.data(), &isSecure, sizeof(int32_t));
+        auto error = hwcLayer->setLayerGenericMetadata(
+                "org.chromium.arc.V1_0.IsSecure", false, val);
+        if (error != hal::Error::NONE) {
+            ALOGW("[%s] Failed to set IsSecure metadata — FLAG_SECURE content may "
+                  "be exposed to screen capture", getLayerFE().getDebugName());
+        }
+    }
+
     writeOutputDependentPerFrameStateToHWC(hwcLayer.get());
     writeOutputIndependentPerFrameStateToHWC(hwcLayer.get(), *outputIndependentState,
                                              requestedCompositionType, skipLayer);
-- 
